README.md
# Institutional Ontology

The Institutional Ontology is the semantic foundation of the Legibility Office Institutional Operating System (IOS).

It defines the vocabulary used throughout the repository.

Everything else builds on the ontology.

```
Ontology

↓

Entities

↓

Relationships

↓

Signals

↓

Patterns

↓

Knowledge Graph

↓

Institutional Intelligence
```

---

## Domains

- Governance
- Procurement
- Digital Public Infrastructure
- Capability
- AI Governance
- Institutional Memory
- Finance
- Risk
- Standards
- Institutions

---

## Supported Standards

- RDF

- OWL

- Turtle

- JSON-LD (future)

- SKOS (future)

- SHACL (future)

---

## Purpose

Provide semantic interoperability for:

- Knowledge Graphs
- AI Systems
- Policy Intelligence
- Institutional Memory
- Semantic Search
- Digital Twins
- Governance Analytics
